      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.25,
      "end_seconds": 10.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "you're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.46,
      "end_seconds": 16.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "um um so... vomiting blood. That's why I came"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.27,
      "end_seconds": 21.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Right, time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.51,
      "end_seconds": 33.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.78,
      "end_seconds": 61.94,
      "duration_seconds": 11.16,
      "text": "okay: heart rate 124, blood pressure 112 over 84, saturation 97 percent, temperature 36.6. Right, what's the the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.49,
      "end_seconds": 71.33,
      "duration_seconds": 7.84,
      "text": "About... well one week. I looked a few things up online and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.51,
      "end_seconds": 74.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "how often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.66,
      "end_seconds": 77.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "honestly, every other day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.65,
      "end_seconds": 82.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.16,
      "end_seconds": 97.65,
      "duration_seconds": 14.49,
      "text": "Stomach pain goes along with it, most of the time. The Stomach pain? That's been for about two weeks. With Stomach pain, I'd give it a five, out of ten"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.88,
      "end_seconds": 118.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "and what about fever or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.49,
      "end_seconds": 126.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "no, none that I've noticed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.08,
      "end_seconds": 131.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.42,
      "end_seconds": 135.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "um nothing on the skin no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.75,
      "end_seconds": 142.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.9,
      "end_seconds": 145.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Nothing odd there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.13,
      "end_seconds": 157.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.88,
      "end_seconds": 162.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "I'm allergic to cat fur, I get sneezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.66,
      "end_seconds": 165.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "how active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.76,
      "end_seconds": 170.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.73,
      "end_seconds": 174.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.28,
      "end_seconds": 180.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.67,
      "end_seconds": 186.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "right, what do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.06,
      "end_seconds": 196.73,
      "duration_seconds": 8.67,
      "text": "Hydrocortisone cream. I take it when needed. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.7,
      "end_seconds": 203.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "what conditions have you been treated for in the the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.13,
      "end_seconds": 205.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "I have eczema"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.06,
      "end_seconds": 210.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "may I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.05,
      "end_seconds": 223.01,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.42,
      "end_seconds": 226.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.17,
      "end_seconds": 242.36,
      "duration_seconds": 7.19,
      "text": "you look pale, your pulse is fast and your tummy is tender at the top"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.38,
      "end_seconds": 261.6,
      "duration_seconds": 14.22,
      "text": "you can relax now right, here's what I'm thinking my working impression is a possible bleeding stomach ulcer i want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.52,
      "end_seconds": 264.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.63,
      "end_seconds": 275.75,
      "duration_seconds": 9.12,
      "text": "it's reasonable to be concerned but right now a possible bleeding stomach ulcer is my leading thought not anything worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.24,
      "end_seconds": 317.93,
      "duration_seconds": 26.69,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an endoscopy for bleeding. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I'm sending you for urgent blood tests because of bleeding. Please stop the ibuprofen and do not eat or drink. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.58,
      "end_seconds": 327.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.25,
      "text": "I'd like you to see the emergency team as well, and I'll write the referral"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.24,
      "end_seconds": 333.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "sure, um, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.57,
      "end_seconds": 341.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "I'll want another look straight away. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.56,
      "end_seconds": 347.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Hmm, good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
